      "message": "Gemini feedback:\n\n----\n\nIn both `BuildEcCommand` and `BuildEcResponse`, you construct a payload by allocating a vector and manually calling `memcpy` multiple times with `sizeof()` math.\n\n```c\nstd::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e packet(sizeof(req) + params.size());\nmemcpy(packet.data(), \u0026req, sizeof(req));\nif (!params.empty()) {\n  memcpy(packet.data() + sizeof(req), params.data(), params.size());\n}\n\n```\n\n**Improvement:** You already wrote a brilliant `AsUint8Span` helper in `ft_util.h` for exact use cases like this\\! You can eliminate the raw pointer math and `memcpy` calls:\n\n```c\nstd::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e packet;\npacket.reserve(sizeof(req) + params.size());\n\nstd::ranges::append_range(packet, AsUint8Span(req));\nstd::ranges::append_range(packet, params);\n```",
