      "message": "Gemini feedback:\n\n----\n\nIn `internal::SendEcCommandAndReadResponse`, there is manual math and an `.insert()` call used to extract the payload from the initial buffer.\n\n```c\nstd::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e response_data;\nsize_t header_size \u003d sizeof(ec_host_response);\nsize_t data_already_received \u003d received - header_size;\nif (data_already_received \u003e 0) {\n  response_data.insert(response_data.end(),\n                       initial_buffer.begin() + header_size,\n                       initial_buffer.begin() + received);\n}\n\n```\n\n**Improvement:** You can delete all of this math and replace it with a single iterator-range constructor. It inherently handles the zero-length case safely:\n\n```c\nstd::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e response_data(\n    initial_buffer.begin() + sizeof(ec_host_response),\n    initial_buffer.begin() + received);\n\n```",
