      "message": "Gemini feedback:\n\n----\n\nCurrently, `UsbTransport::Send()` and `Recv()` return an `int`. This forces your higher-level business logic in `ft_scsi.cc` to constantly do things like:\n\n```c\nif (*send_res !\u003d static_cast\u003cint\u003e(data_buffer.size())) { ... }\n\n```\n\nThe only reason `Send`/`Recv` return `int` is because the underlying `libusb_bulk_transfer` API uses `int`. But your custom transport interface should be agnostic to libusb\\!\n\n**Improvement:** Change `UsbTransport::Send` and `Recv` to return `std::expected\u003csize_t, Error\u003e`. Confine the `static_cast` to the return statement inside `LibusbTransport::Send/Recv`. This completely eliminates all the `static_cast\u003cint\u003e` boilerplate polluting `ft_scsi.cc` and `usb_device_test.cc`, making your USB abstractions purely `size_t` native.",
