      "message": "Gemini feedback:\n\n-----\n\nIn `DownloadBin`, when handling the final trailing bytes of the firmware, you allocate a `std::vector` on the heap just to pad it with `0xFF`:\n\n```c\nif (!remaining_data.empty()) {\n  std::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e final_chunk(remaining_data.begin(), remaining_data.end());\n  final_chunk.resize(kFocalConfigSize, 0xFF);\n  // ...\n}\n\n```\n\n**Improvement:** Because `kFocalConfigSize` is exactly 4096 bytes, this is incredibly safe to do on the stack. Using `std::array` here completely eliminates dynamic heap allocations during the flash write loop:\n\n```c\nif (!remaining_data.empty()) {\n  std::array\u003cuint8_t, kFocalConfigSize\u003e final_chunk;\n  final_chunk.fill(0xFF);\n  std::ranges::copy(remaining_data, final_chunk.begin());\n  \n  auto page_res \u003d DownloadPage(device, downaddr, final_chunk.size(), final_chunk);\n  if (!page_res) return page_res;\n}\n\n```",
