      "message": "Gemini feedback:\n\n----\n\nIn `VerifyData`, you compare the local SHA256 hash with the device\u0027s hash using `std::ranges`:\n\n```c\nauto local_hash \u003d CalculateSha256(firmware_data);\nif (!std::ranges::equal(local_hash, device_hash)) { ... }\n\n```\n\n**Improvement:** Because both arrays are strictly defined as `std::array\u003cuint8_t, 32\u003e`, you do not need ranges or loops here. `std::array` implements `operator\u003d\u003d` natively, which is cleaner and often optimizes better:\n\n```c\nif (local_hash !\u003d device_hash) { \n    FT_LOGE(\"Hash mismatch...\");\n    return std::unexpected(Error::kResultFail); \n}\n\n```",
